==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|bruk-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bʰrūg-|enjoy|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''brūka'', Old High German ''brūhhan'' (German [[brauchen]]), Old Saxon ''brūkan'' (Dutch [[bruiken]]), Gothic [[𐌱𐍂𐌿𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽]].  The IE root was also the source of Latin [[frui]] ‘enjoy’ and [[frux]] ‘fruit’.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|/ˈbruːcɑn/}}

===Verb===
{{Latinx|'''brūcan'''}}

# to [[enjoy]], to make use of
# to [[digest]] food

